<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Validated Mathematics of Biological Form" ;
    skos:narrower <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain-3> .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Grieneisen et al. (2007) Vascular-Epidermal Counter-Current Reflux Conservation Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves exact internal cancellation of lateral reflux transfer between outer tissues and vascular stele and counter-current flux balance J_{stele} + J_{epidermis} = 0 at a closed root tip boundary, explaining why the root tip reflux capacitor remains self-sustaining after shoot decapitation (J_{in} = 0) | Variables: A_s, A_e: vascular stele and epidermal/cortical auxin concentrations; J_s, J_e: rootward PIN1 stele flux and shootward PIN2 epidermal flux; k_{lat}: inward lateral PIN1/PIN2/PIN3 reflux rate across cortex/endodermis; μ: basal auxin turnover rate" ;
    dct:source "Grieneisen, Xu, Marée, Hogeweg & Scheres (2007) Nature 449(7165):1008-1013 Eqs. 1-4 & Fig. 3" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/2014-grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain.py#L105-L215>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_038_root_auxin_reflux_fountain.lean#L31-L53> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def stele_reflux_rhs (dJ_s k_lat A_e mu A_s : Int) : Int :=
  -dJ_s + k_lat * A_e - mu * A_s
def epidermis_reflux_rhs (dJ_e k_lat A_e mu : Int) : Int :=
  -dJ_e - k_lat * A_e - mu * A_e
theorem grieneisen_2007_vascular_epidermal_reflux_conservation
    (dJ_s dJ_e k_lat A_s A_e mu J_tip : Int) :
    stele_reflux_rhs dJ_s k_lat A_e mu A_s + epidermis_reflux_rhs dJ_e k_lat A_e mu =
      -(dJ_s + dJ_e) - mu * (A_s + A_e) ∧
    stele_reflux_rhs dJ_s k_lat A_e 0 A_s + epidermis_reflux_rhs (-dJ_s) k_lat A_e 0 = 0 ∧
    cross_section_net_flux J_tip (-J_tip) = 0
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "∂A_s/∂t + ∂A_e/∂t = (-∂J_s/∂z + k_{lat} A_e - μ A_s) + (-∂J_e/∂z - k_{lat} A_e - μ A_e) = -∂(J_s + J_e)/∂z - μ(A_s + A_e),   J_{stele}(0) + J_{epidermis}(0) = 0  (μ = 0, J_{in} = 0)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0092-8674(00)81535-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature03184>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature06215>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature13663> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "2D Anisotropic Vascular–Epidermal Polar PIN1/PIN2/PIN3 Advection-Diffusion Reflux Loop & Quiescent Center (QC) Exponential Capacitor" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_038.stele_reflux_rhs" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_038.grieneisen_2007_vascular_epidermal_reflux_conservation" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Grieneisen et al. (2007) Quiescent Center (QC) Reflux Capacitor Amplification vs NPA / Lateral-PIN Ablation Collapse Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves that simultaneous rootward PIN1 advection (v_s > 0), shootward PIN2 advection (v_e > 0), and inward lateral reflux (k_{lat} > 0) strictly amplify distal Quiescent Center auxin concentration above the shoot boundary, whereas lateral PIN ablation (k_{lat} = 0) or NPA polar transport blockade (v_s = v_e = 0) collapses the capacitor to the unamplified baseline | Variables: A_{QC}: distal Quiescent Center auxin concentration; A_{shoot}: proximal shootward boundary auxin concentration; v_s: rootward stele PIN1 velocity; v_e: shootward epidermal PIN2 velocity; k_{lat}: inward lateral reflux rate; λ_{QC}: effective reflux capacitor decay length" ;
    dct:source "Grieneisen, Xu, Marée, Hogeweg & Scheres (2007) Nature 449(7165):1008-1013 Figs. 1-3" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/2014-grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain.py#L218-L410>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_038_root_auxin_reflux_fountain.lean#L70-L92> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def qc_two_stage_capacitor (A_shoot v_s v_e k_lat : Int) : Int :=
  A_shoot * (1 + v_s * v_e * k_lat) * (1 + v_s * v_e * k_lat)
theorem grieneisen_2007_qc_capacitor_amplification_vs_collapse
    (A_shoot v_s v_e k_lat : Int)
    (hA : A_shoot > 0) (hvs : v_s > 0) (hve : v_e > 0) (hklat : k_lat > 0) :
    qc_two_stage_capacitor A_shoot v_s v_e k_lat > A_shoot ∧
    qc_two_stage_capacitor A_shoot v_s v_e 0 = A_shoot ∧
    qc_two_stage_capacitor A_shoot 0 0 k_lat = A_shoot
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "A_{QC} / A_{shoot} = exp(L / λ_{QC}) ≫ 1  (v_s > 0, v_e > 0, k_{lat} > 0)   vs   A_{QC} / A_{shoot} = 1  (k_{lat} = 0  ∨  v_s = v_e = 0)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0092-8674(00)81535-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature03184>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature06215>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature13663> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "2D Anisotropic Vascular–Epidermal Polar PIN1/PIN2/PIN3 Advection-Diffusion Reflux Loop & Quiescent Center (QC) Exponential Capacitor" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_038.qc_two_stage_capacitor" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_038.grieneisen_2007_qc_capacitor_amplification_vs_collapse" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Mähönen et al. (2014) PLETHORA (PLT1/2) Dosage Gradient & Meristem Boundary Monotonicity Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves that higher reflux capacitor gain G_{reflux} strictly elevates PLETHORA dosage across the root apex and shifts the Meristem-to-Elongation Zone boundary z_{MZ} shootward, explaining progressive meristem shrinkage across WT > decapitated > pin2 > lateral-pin ablation > NPA blockade | Variables: P(z): axial PLETHORA (PLT1/PLT2) transcription factor concentration at distance z from the root tip; G_{reflux}: QC auxin reflux capacitor gain; α_{plt}: auxin-induced PLT synthesis rate; β_{decay}: axial PLT dilution/decay slope; Θ_{MZ}: PLT dosage threshold separating Meristematic Zone from Elongation Zone; z_{MZ}: Meristematic Zone boundary coordinate" ;
    dct:source "Mähönen et al. (2014) Nature 515(7525):125-129 Figs. 1-4; Grieneisen et al. (2007) Nature 449:1008-1013 Fig. 2" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/2014-grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain.py#L413-L520>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_038_root_auxin_reflux_fountain.lean#L108-L128> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def plethora_axial_dosage (alpha_plt G_reflux beta_decay z : Int) : Int :=
  alpha_plt * G_reflux - beta_decay * z
def meristem_boundary_coord (alpha_plt G_reflux Theta_MZ : Int) : Int :=
  alpha_plt * G_reflux - Theta_MZ
theorem mahonen_2014_plethora_meristem_boundary_monotonicity
    (alpha_plt G1 G2 beta_decay z Theta_MZ : Int)
    (h_alpha : alpha_plt > 0) (h_gain : G2 > G1) :
    plethora_axial_dosage alpha_plt G2 beta_decay z >
      plethora_axial_dosage alpha_plt G1 beta_decay z ∧
    meristem_boundary_coord alpha_plt G2 Theta_MZ >
      meristem_boundary_coord alpha_plt G1 Theta_MZ
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "G_2 > G_1 ∧ α_{plt} > 0  ⇒  P(z; G_2) > P(z; G_1)  ∧  z_{MZ}(G_2) > z_{MZ}(G_1)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0092-8674(00)81535-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature03184>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature06215>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature13663> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "2D Anisotropic Vascular–Epidermal Polar PIN1/PIN2/PIN3 Advection-Diffusion Reflux Loop & Quiescent Center (QC) Exponential Capacitor" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_038.plethora_axial_dosage" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_038.mahonen_2014_plethora_meristem_boundary_monotonicity" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "MorphoEval simulation-faithfulness rubric v0.1.0" ;
    dct:description "Weighted 0-100 rubric for the faithfulness of a morphology simulation to its organism and source model; Overall = weighted mean. Each score is a pk:LLMClaimAssessment (ProbKnow rubric-assessment template) of the pk:Claim pkr:claim/morphoeval-<sim> against one dimension (dct:subject the dimension concept, pk:assessmentType morphoeval/<version>/<dimension>) with pk:hasScore = score/100 — an uncalibrated rubric score, not a probability — and a pk:hasVerdict band; the overall score has the rubric itself as dct:subject and is also the pk:weightOfEvidence of the claim." ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/morphoeval/rubric.yaml> ;
    skos:narrower <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> .

